        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"shakespeare-king-lear-afbd3a1978a723e3\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.97,\"analysis\":\"Goneril’s “I love you” is grammatically and pragmatically an avowal that presents her filial love as an existing state, elaborated through hyperbolic comparisons. The competitive and likely strategic setting affects its sincerity but not its strong truth-conditional mode. It neither clearly undertakes a commitment nor functions as a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"Goneril may possess some ordinary filial affection, but the passage strongly suggests that the extravagant degree claimed is strategically exaggerated. This sincerity question does not alter the core T classification.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Goneril directly addresses Lear during his public test of which daughter professes the greatest love; the highlighted opening avowal is reiterated at the end of her prepared rhetorical speech.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Lear explicitly solicits competing declarations of love and ties the greatest profession to the largest territorial bounty. Goneril responds first with an elaborate, hyperbolic avowal and is immediately rewarded with land. Cordelia’s asides and later objection that her sisters also owe love to their husbands cast doubt on the claimed totality of Goneril’s devotion. The declaration therefore appears calculated and self-interested, but manipulation and possible insincerity remain contextual features of an utterance whose core force is still assertive/avowal-like.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Sir, I love you more than word can wield the matter”\",\"supports\":\"The utterance directly presents Goneril’s love for Lear, and its exceptional degree, as true; this strongly supports T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Goneril develops the claim through comparisons including “Dearer than eyesight, space, and liberty” and “No less than life.”\",\"supports\":\"The sustained comparisons elaborate the asserted magnitude of her love rather than supplying evidence of a commitment or reflex-like discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Lear asks which daughter “doth love us most” so that he may extend his “largest bounty,” and grants Goneril a rich portion immediately after her speech.\",\"supports\":\"The declaration occurs in a competitive, materially consequential love test, supporting a strategic or flattering contextual interpretation without changing its truth-conditional mode.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Cordelia responds aside, “What shall Cordelia speak? Love, and be silent,” and later challenges the sisters’ claim to love Lear wholly when they have husbands.\",\"supports\":\"Cordelia’s contrast casts doubt on the sincerity or accuracy of Goneril’s hyperbolic profession.\",\"confidence\":0.95},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The avowal forms part of a long, syntactically controlled public speech that culminates in “Beyond all manner of so much I love you.”\",\"supports\":\"The deliberate rhetorical construction weighs against treating the words as an independently reflex-like expressive discharge; emotional language alone does not establish E.\",\"confidence\":0.96}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. Its hyperbole, probable calculation, and disputed sincerity are adequately represented as contextual qualifications; no important core force remains outside T/P/E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
